1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,800
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,140
(Yu Yang & Liang Renfang's
Stargazing Room Date)

14
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,600
Didn't you say
you wanted to make a song?

15
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:43,060
(Yu Yang's sampler)
It's kind of like a calculator.

16
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,000
It can actually do a lot of things.

17
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,800
I just wanted to record some sounds.

18
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:56,480
Like this one.

19
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:57,920
I really wanted to record this.

20
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:06,800
Liang Renfang.

21
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,160
Haha!

22
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,400
Haha.

23
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,400
How did it turn
into a completely different sound?

24
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,760
Are we really using this?

25
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,080
Oh my.

26
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,120
Help.

27
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,120
Are we really using this?

28
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,920
Your voice will stay

29
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,520
on my computer forever.

30
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,600
This sounds kind of like raindrops.

31
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,520
I'll change the setting.

32
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,920
It'll sound even more like raindrops.

33
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,920
It sounds like a heartbeat.

34
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,200
Yeah.

35
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,120
Try pressing it a few times.

36
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,720
Anything else?

37
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:10,600
Can I

38
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,200
press that "3"?

39
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,440
Sure.

40
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:13,920
"3".

41
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:15,440
Try pressing it down.

42
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,540
(Glances)

43
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,320
Like this.

44
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,680
Can you keep pressing this for me?

45
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:30,280
Okay.

46
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,480
Let's work together for a bit.

47
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,720
I feel like my heartbeat

48
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:43,840
is starting to match its rhythm.

49
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:48,500
Okay.

50
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:52,000
Let's add something else.

51
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,600
Can you...

52
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,480
Sing?

53
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,560
What should I sing?

54
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,520
Or, no.

55
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,400
You don't need lyrics.

56
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,500
Just follow the melody

57
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,780
and improvise a little.

58
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:08,860
Let me think.

59
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,420
Don't worry about getting it
right or wrong.

60
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,060
Because it doesn't matter.

61
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,340
There's no right or wrong.

62
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,060
That one. The one you just did.

63
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,860
I heard it.

64
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,420
(Happy)

65
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,220
Come on.

66
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,420
The sound of a fairy.

67
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:52,740
A fairy. Your voice.

68
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,980
(Glances)

69
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:35,900
My arm's sore.

70
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:38,620
You just fell asleep.

71
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,260
Took a rest.

72
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,100
Did it leave a red mark?

73
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:47,580
No.

74
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,180
(Praise)
You're so handsome.

75
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,340
You're so handsome.

76
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,900
(Glances)

77
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:04,860
Are you cold?

78
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:05,980
A little, but I'm okay.

79
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,340
Let's get a blanket.

80
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,420
Okay.

81
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:12,540
(Looks back)

82
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,140
Is there one?

83
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:25,700
Thank you.

84
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:27,460
So warm.

85
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:36,940
Hold this.

86
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,020
What is this?

87
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:43,900
Who left this here?

88
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:45,900
There's also this.

89
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,700
The one for writing on the blackboard.

90
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:51,340
You can draw on this.

91
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:54,260
I'll draw a little bunny.

92
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,060
Okay.

93
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:57,340
The little bunny in front of us.

94
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:06,460
So do you get nervous
when someone watches you draw?

95
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,700
No.

96
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,660
I used to teach kids.

97
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:12,820
Really?

98
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:17,460
Elementary and middle school students.

99
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,860
What did you teach them to draw?

100
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:21,900
Sketching or something else?

101
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:22,700
Sketching.

102
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:26,060
What did you start with
when you first learned to sketch?

103
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:28,340
Cubes.

104
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:29,700
Just drawing cubes?

105
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:31,300
Didn't you find it boring

106
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,580
when you were learning?

107
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,500
Or did you find it fun?

108
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:35,740
I found it fun.

109
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:36,940
I thought turning something

110
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:40,700
into a three-dimensional drawing
was really fun.

111
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:46,380
It's okay. I'll wipe it with my hand.

112
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,540
No, I want to help too.

113
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,140
Right?

114
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,700
(Leans closer)
Right?

115
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:58,540
Like putting on blush.

116
00:06:58,540 --> 00:06:59,860
What is this?

117
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:03,420
Should this ear be pink too?

118
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:04,420
Yeah.

119
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,140
What is this?

120
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:08,780
This is...

121
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,540
This is its...

122
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:12,700
This is the mouth and philtrum.

123
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,100
Is it supposed to be red?

124
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,300
Can we color its clothes?

125
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,180
I can color them.

126
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,300
Sure.

127
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,100
The color is really even.

128
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:35,980
Not bad.

129
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:37,660
(Smiles)

130
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:38,660
Pretty good, right?

131
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,780
Of course.

132
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:40,540
How is it?

133
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:41,940
I've got some technique too.

134
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:43,740
But what do I do
if the middle part is gone?

135
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,540
That's okay. Color it first.

136
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:46,780
Once you're done...

137
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:48,380
You'll draw it in.

138
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,180
Right.

139
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:50,900
Does this work?

140
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:51,700
Yep.

141
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:52,580
(Brings it up)
Mr. Cao.

142
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,380
There.

143
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:08,940
Not bad.

144
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:09,420
Now

145
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:12,180
you can officially sign your name on it.

146
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:12,980
Think about it.

147
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,980
Can we add a little blush?

148
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:18,500
Would this work?

149
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:19,260
Yep.

150
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:21,340
Let's come up with an artist name.

151
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:23,980
How about it?

152
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:27,380
Put both our last names on it.

153
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,140
Sure.

154
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:32,220
This looks like an emoji.

155
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:35,980
You have no idea what it is, do you?
Pretty clever, huh?

156
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,980
I'm so smart.

157
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:40,460
Where should we put it?

158
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,620
Just put it on this table.

159
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,260
This could be a hair clip.

160
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:48,620
Sure.

161
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:50,380
Not bad.

162
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,620
I remember that day.

163
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,060
The day we went out together.

164
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,780
You wore dark green.

165
00:08:58,780 --> 00:08:59,860
Dark green.

166
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,620
Then the next day, you wore light green.

167
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:02,780
Both looked really good on you.

168
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:05,980
Thanks. Yellow looks really good on you.

169
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:08,220
Yellow makes you look so sunny.

170
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,740
(Laughs)

171
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:13,340
So do you think you're the type
to fall in love at first sight,

172
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,460
or fall for someone over time?

173
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:17,620
To be honest,

174
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:21,220
I used to think
I'd fall for someone over time.

175
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:23,300
But I guess
I can fall in love at first sight.

176
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,020
I mean, when I came to Signal House,

177
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:27,300
everything felt so magical.

178
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:31,340
It's more about enjoying

179
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:34,180
the little time we have left
at Signal House.

180
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:42,940
Let's take this upstairs and eat.

181
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:43,940
Let's go together.

182
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:44,700
Sure.

183
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:45,380
Let's go.

184
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,420
Do you want some of this?

185
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:49,380
I'll spray a little. Thanks.

186
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:52,460
(Reaches out)
How about we each take a pillow?

187
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:52,940
Sure.

188
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:54,940
It's cold.

189
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:57,940
I feel like we should spray some.

190
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:59,260
Here, spray some.

191
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,480
I'm good. It's fine.

192
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:01,580
You want to be
an "automatic" mosquito repellent?

193
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:02,620
I've got plenty of blood. I'm fine.

194
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,900
You guys haven't had any fruit yet.

195
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:10,300
Come on.

196
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:13,380
(Laughs)

197
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:14,580
Perfect, one fork each.

198
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:16,740
One blue, one pink.

199
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:17,500
You two can pick.

200
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,660
No, we can just share this one.

201
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:22,540
Actually, you can take one.

202
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:23,460
Okay, we...

203
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,420
We can just use one.

204
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:25,180
Here.

205
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,020
You go first.

206
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:27,180
Do you want me to feed you?

207
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:28,140
Sure, why not.

208
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,180
Why didn't you feed me?

209
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:34,940
(Laughs)

210
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,580
When are you two going on a city date?

211
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:44,460
Why didn't you ask me out?

212
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:46,500
I...

213
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:48,660
You've been a little stingy lately.

214
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:49,100
Yeah.

215
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:50,540
You've been

216
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:52,460
a little "stingy" lately.

217
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,380
You're saving those Coins
in your hand, right?

218
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:57,860
(Laughing)

219
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:01,340
Ask him.

220
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,500
Which one Cui Yihang wants to pick.

221
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,060
Can I take a guess?

222
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:07,820
City date.

223
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,700
Definitely a city date.

224
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:12,980
What about you?

225
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,420
There are quite a few places
I'd like to go.

226
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,300
But the places I'm thinking of

227
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,700
aren't really that fun.

228
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,340
You can think about it.

229
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,540
Maybe somewhere from my childhood.

230
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:23,820
But that place was torn down.

231
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:24,980
Though maybe there's still

232
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,500
a little piece of it left.

233
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,580
I think that's a great idea.

234
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:32,540
You could tell the stories
from your childhood.

235
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,340
That sounds really nice.

236
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:40,140
You know what?

237
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:41,540
Liang Xiaoyu has always
given me this feeling.

238
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,580
Whenever we talk about something,

239
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:45,220
she never argues back.

240
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:46,020
She's always there.

241
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:47,660
(Always giving validation)

242
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,620
That's because I really like your idea.

243
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,940
Yeah, you probably just agree.

244
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:51,260
Yeah.

245
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:56,140
I'd really like to find somewhere

246
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:57,540
a little closer to nature,

247
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:58,780
where the two of us can just sit

248
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:00,020
and maybe talk.

249
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,460
I think that'd be really nice.

250
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,560
(Ask)
Do you think the stargazing room

251
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,900
is a good place to talk?

252
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:09,700
It could give you

253
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,180
a really private space.

254
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:11,900
You can just talk,

255
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:13,420
or have other kinds of interactions,

256
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,420
like using the telescope.

257
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,300
The astronomical telescope.

258
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:17,060
There are probably things

259
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:18,460
you wouldn't feel comfortable
asking around others,

260
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:19,720
or just can't bring yourself to ask.

261
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,660
But when it's just the two of you,

262
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:21,980
you can get to know each other better.

263
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:25,060
But I think it's crucial to get
to know each other at first.

264
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:31,260
It seems like you were there
for over four hours.

265
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:37,580
Did you hear that?

266
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:38,940
He waited for you for over four hours.

267
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:39,620
You missed me?

268
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,260
No.

269
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,740
I like joking around.

270
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,100
I love watching you two joke around.

271
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:51,500
They treat us like a "show".

272
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,580
(Joking)
And this one charges a fee.

273
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:54,580
This one charges a fee.

274
00:12:58,900 --> 00:12:59,840
No fee is fine too.

275
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:00,560
(Joke failed)

276
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:00,960
It's fine.

277
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:05,140
No fee is fine too.

278
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,180
Let me take a photo of you two.

279
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:09,980
One for each of you.

280
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:10,860
That's a good idea.

281
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:11,740
Yeah, sure.

282
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:13,940
Let me take a look.

283
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:14,980
Relax a little, okay?

284
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:15,420
Just relax.

285
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:16,460
Give me a peace sign.

286
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:21,020
Get ready.

287
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:23,380
One, two, three.

288
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,220
You two look so good in this one.

289
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,380
Thanks.

290
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:29,660
One,

291
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:31,140
two,

292
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:32,100
three.

293
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:33,940
I look great in this one.

294
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:34,940
This one is really good.

295
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:37,300
I'll go in first.

296
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,100
You two hang out for a bit.

297
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:38,900
Okay.

298
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,420
Do you have photos with everyone?

299
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:45,860
Last time, I took some with Zhao Xilun

300
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,300
and Sun Bohan.

301
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:49,380
I'm going too.

302
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:50,340
You stay here for a bit.

303
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:51,980
I'm gonna walk around.

304
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:55,100
(Show)

305
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:55,460
What's this?

306
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,340
Can I take a look, Chen Hewen?

307
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,340
Sure, we took some photos earlier.

308
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:58,300
Thank you.

309
00:13:58,300 --> 00:13:59,540
We just took some photos.

310
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:01,980
You have the heart pillows.

311
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,220
Go stick them on the fridge.

312
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:05,540
Can we stick them to the fridge?

313
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:06,260
Of course.

314
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:06,820
Okay.

315
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:07,540
Chen Hewen,

316
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:09,300
when you went
to the stargazing room that day,

317
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,820
Sun Bohan and I took several photos.

318
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,060
We can take photos in there.

319
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,020
They have a camera now.

320
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:13,620
Yeah.

321
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,060
Let's go take some photos.

322
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:17,780
Can you take one for us?

323
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:18,980
We haven't taken a photo together yet.

324
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:19,420
Yeah.

325
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,260
I think you two should sit here.

326
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:22,220
Okay.

327
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:23,500
We looked pretty good here just now.

328
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:26,020
Let's take one each.

329
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:26,660
One pillow each.

330
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,460
Let's take one each.

331
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,300
I think we have to take this.

332
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:28,540
Come on.

333
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:29,220
Yeah.

334
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:30,620
One pillow each.

335
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,420
One, two, three.

336
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:39,380
Meng, you two take one.

337
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:40,060
Yeah.

338
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,100
Take a photo.

339
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:43,020
You take one.

340
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:43,740
We'll take one too.

341
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:44,540
Sure.

342
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:46,740
Okay.

343
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:47,700
Sure.

344
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:49,540
(Get closer)

345
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:53,180
One, two, three.

346
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:54,980
That looks pretty good.

347
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:55,980
Really.

348
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:56,540
We both

349
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:57,340
look great in this one.

350
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,420
This one looks great.

351
00:14:58,740 --> 00:14:59,300
Come on.

352
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:01,840
One, two, three.

353
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:07,780
Are you ready?

354
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:09,580
Ready.

355
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,940
One, two, three.

356
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:19,460
Three,

357
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:20,860
two,

358
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:21,980
one.

359
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,020
Now that's a great shot.

360
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,060
You nailed it.

361
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,180
Just like a "master".

362
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,540
Let's do serious faces.

363
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:28,300
Okay.

364
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,100
We're...

365
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,300
- Perfect.
- Quiet beauties.

366
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:30,950
Perfect.

367
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:33,240
Three, two, one.

368
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,540
Should we stick them on the fridge?

369
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,180
Yeah, let's put them on the fridge.

370
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:40,340
Okay.

371
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:41,260
Sure.

372
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:41,500
Okay.

373
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,460
Let's go.

374
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:43,260
Go, go, go.

375
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,820
(The next day)

376
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,540
Come on, let's play badminton.

377
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:52,700
Come on.

378
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,540
You can't really play in those.

379
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:55,980
You're wearing flip-flops.

380
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:57,980
Liang Xiaoyu is wearing flip-flops too.

381
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:00,180
(Glances)

382
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:04,140
(Gesture)

383
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:06,860
Let's play for a bit. Come on.

384
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:11,380
Sorry.

385
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:12,820
I need to watch my strength.

386
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,500
I'm in flip-flops. Go easy on me.

387
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,020
Mine.

388
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,140
I can't reach it.

389
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,500
Do you want to play for a bit?

390
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,980
Let's switch off. Come on.

391
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,340
(Inviting)

392
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:29,700
Sure.

393
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:32,740
Do you want to play for a bit?

394
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:35,820
Okay.

395
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,580
Do you want to play together?

396
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:42,940
Want to play together?

397
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:43,540
Let's play together.

398
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:44,540
Come on.

399
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:47,740
(Five people, four rackets)

400
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,020
I'll watch.

401
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,300
It's kind of dangerous.

402
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,460
I'll stand back.

403
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:56,380
You want to play? Go ahead.

404
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:57,500
It's fine. I'll just watch.

405
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:05,020
(Hands it over)

406
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:10,100
Come on.

407
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:16,300
(Takes it)

408
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:17,900
The blanket...

409
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,260
Hold this for me.

410
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:21,660
Thanks.

411
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:28,220
We can use

412
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:29,820
that yellow line

413
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:30,380
as the boundary.

414
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,180
You guys play over there.

415
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,740
You go.

416
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:37,780
I'll grab a chair and watch.

417
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:38,820
You play. I'll referee.

418
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:39,820
Come on.

419
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:41,940
(Hands it over)

420
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:43,860
Okay, then I'll...

421
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,340
show off a little.

422
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:51,500
Over here?

423
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,740
(Looks)

424
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,220
I think so.

425
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:56,220
Three against one?

426
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:56,740
We can...

427
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:57,740
Let's do two-on-two.

428
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:00,300
I'll stand here.

429
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:00,940
Don't want to hit you.

430
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:01,900
Okay.

431
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:03,140
I just...

432
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:06,620
Why am I playing against you?

433
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,500
Come on, you'll be fine.

434
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,060
Don't worry. I'll cover you.

435
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:16,860
(Misses)

436
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,820
The white team's giving you a chance.

437
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:31,780
(Swings at it)

438
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:32,900
Don't look up.

439
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,180
You don't have to hit it that hard.

440
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:37,740
(Imitates)

441
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,060
I didn't even hit it hard.

442
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,420
You closed your eyes.

443
00:19:05,460 --> 00:19:06,540
You're doing all the work here.

444
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,380
He keeps sending everything your way.

445
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:24,460
That didn't clear.

446
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:25,820
We need that in slow-mo.

447
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:27,300
That was smooth.

448
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,580
That last one

449
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,100
that was ours, right?

450
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:30,540
Yeah.

451
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:34,480
High five.

452
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,200
(High-fives with racket)

453
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:36,580
Nice! Come on.

454
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:42,460
You even have a victory pose.

455
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,500
Yeah.

456
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:50,420
Oh, my bad.

457
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:52,380
You're doing great.

458
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:55,620
(Smashes)

459
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:58,380
I feel like...

460
00:19:58,940 --> 00:19:59,860
I swear she's trying

461
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:01,660
to take me out with that racket.

462
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:04,820
You caught me.

463
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:13,900
Sorry!

464
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:16,820
(Panicked)
Sorry!

465
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,060
That was good, huh?

466
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:19,940
I'm sorry.

467
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:20,580
(Apologize again)

468
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,260
That's a foul.

469
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:24,020
You got a penalty.

470
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:27,060
Sorry.

471
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,340
That shot of hers was really...

472
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:38,660
Do I get two tries, ref?

473
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,500
Sure.

474
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:44,540
Let's take a break.

475
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:44,900
Okay.

476
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:45,700
Sure.

477
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:49,620
You tired?

478
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:50,860
I'm okay.

479
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:52,780
So many mosquitoes here.

480
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:54,260
Let's go back up.

481
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:55,780
I'll go first.

482
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:57,340
Okay. I'll steady it.

483
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,020
I'll pull you up.

484
00:20:58,020 --> 00:20:59,060
Don't let the boat drift.

485
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:01,820
Can you get up?

486
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:03,340
Yeah, one sec.

487
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:04,540
It's okay. I'm holding onto this.

488
00:21:04,540 --> 00:21:05,420
(Grabs hold)

489
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:06,900
Okay.

490
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:10,500
(Pulls)

491
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,540
Okay.

492
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,700
Okay. Let's go.

493
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:14,860
That was tough, huh?

494
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,060
Let's go.

495
00:21:17,060 --> 00:21:17,860
Okay. Let's go.

496
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,780
I might need to change my socks.

497
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:24,020
They got wet, huh?

498
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,100
Xing, did your shoes get wet?

499
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:28,500
Wipe them off when we get back.

500
00:21:28,980 --> 00:21:29,860
Okay.

501
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:32,460
Xing, I'll wait...

502
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:33,260
- Okay.
- Here.

503
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:46,940
(Freshens up)

504
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,580
(Sprays on more perfume)

505
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,580
(Waits)

506
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:13,420
(Freshens up)

507
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:17,260
(Freshens up +1)

508
00:22:20,300 --> 00:22:22,260
(Freshens up +2)

509
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,980
Xing, I grabbed you some tea.

510
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:46,260
You have it. I'm good.

511
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:50,940
A mosquito got me by the eye.

512
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:51,420
Really?

513
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:52,780
(Leans closer)

514
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:53,380
Right here.

515
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:56,300
See it?

516
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:57,580
Yep, that's a bite.

517
00:22:58,420 --> 00:22:59,580
So annoying.

518
00:23:00,020 --> 00:23:00,700
(Looks)

519
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:02,580
Did you get bit here too?

520
00:23:02,860 --> 00:23:03,740
Here?

521
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:04,540
Here.

522
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:05,820
Here.

523
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:10,300
No, it's a pimple.

524
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,980
I thought it was a bite.

525
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:15,340
These mosquitoes are vicious.

526
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:22,060
Where are you sore?

527
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:23,100
Shoulders? Neck?

528
00:23:23,420 --> 00:23:25,260
We can adjust where it massages, right?

529
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:26,380
Yeah, I think so.

530
00:23:26,380 --> 00:23:27,860
I haven't figured it out.

531
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:29,420
I barely use this chair.

532
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,380
When I first started riding,

533
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:39,540
my back hurt for like a week after.

534
00:23:39,540 --> 00:23:41,420
It just wouldn't stop hurting.

535
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:43,500
I didn't know how to ride.

536
00:23:44,620 --> 00:23:46,340
Maybe your balance was off.

537
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:49,460
Yeah. Honestly, I'm still not that good.

538
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:53,420
I'm just really into it.

539
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:55,700
After the show, maybe...

540
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:58,540
maybe we could learn together.

541
00:23:58,540 --> 00:23:59,060
Sure.

542
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:00,060
(Sure)

543
00:24:04,820 --> 00:24:06,220
Who's playing piano?

544
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:07,340
It's Liang Xiaoyu. She's playing downstairs.

545
00:24:13,980 --> 00:24:15,250
So relaxing.

546
00:24:18,220 --> 00:24:19,940
(Smiles)

547
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:21,900
Just lying here getting a massage

548
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:23,940
while a friend plays piano downstairs.

549
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:32,100
Xing, where else do you like
to hang out?

550
00:24:32,100 --> 00:24:32,980
Besides the park.

551
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:35,660
I like hanging out with kids.

552
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:39,300
You like people-watching?

553
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:39,940
People-watching?

554
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:41,180
Like sitting in the park

555
00:24:41,180 --> 00:24:42,580
watching people go by.

556
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:43,460
I do.

557
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:45,620
So you like quiet spots?

558
00:24:46,180 --> 00:24:48,620
I like lively places too.

559
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:51,620
With the right company, right?

560
00:24:51,620 --> 00:24:52,420
Yeah.

561
00:24:57,740 --> 00:24:59,140
Feels kind of like home.

562
00:24:59,140 --> 00:24:59,860
Yeah.

563
00:25:00,460 --> 00:25:01,100
This is nice.

564
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:05,980
Hi.

565
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:06,740
Hello.

566
00:25:06,740 --> 00:25:07,620
Hello, Meng.

567
00:25:09,020 --> 00:25:10,980
Kind of chilly today.

568
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,100
Even when we're quiet,

569
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:19,100
it's never awkward.

570
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:21,180
Yeah. No pressure.

571
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:23,780
We don't always have to reply.

572
00:25:23,780 --> 00:25:25,740
I like that too.

573
00:25:30,380 --> 00:25:32,500
When you first came,

574
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:34,980
I didn't think I'd get asked out.

575
00:25:34,980 --> 00:25:36,940
Thought it was just an activity?

576
00:25:36,940 --> 00:25:38,260
Yeah, I thought it'd be

577
00:25:38,260 --> 00:25:39,660
some group thing.

578
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:40,380
I didn't expect...

579
00:25:41,620 --> 00:25:41,980
Yeah.

580
00:25:41,980 --> 00:25:45,220
I didn't expect fate to do this.

581
00:25:48,340 --> 00:25:49,140
Did you ask her

582
00:25:49,140 --> 00:25:50,140
why she picked me?

583
00:25:50,460 --> 00:25:51,180
Did she say

584
00:25:51,180 --> 00:25:52,580
I'm kind of goofy and clueless?

585
00:25:52,940 --> 00:25:53,820
No, nothing like that.

586
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:56,420
She said you're a good guy.

587
00:25:57,060 --> 00:25:58,740
I just want to be...

588
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:01,660
as genuine as I can.

589
00:26:01,820 --> 00:26:04,060
People notice when you're genuine.

590
00:26:04,060 --> 00:26:04,580
Yeah.

591
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:10,060
Have you been to the safari park?

592
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:12,740
I've been twice,

593
00:26:12,740 --> 00:26:13,740
but never saw the whole thing.

594
00:26:15,180 --> 00:26:16,580
Then let's go to the zoo.

595
00:26:17,300 --> 00:26:18,500
(Leans in)
The zoo.

596
00:26:18,740 --> 00:26:19,620
The zoo.

597
00:26:20,460 --> 00:26:21,820
Still the zoo?

598
00:26:24,340 --> 00:26:25,060
Okay.

599
00:26:25,060 --> 00:26:25,820
(Looks)

600
00:26:26,060 --> 00:26:27,220
I want to see the animals.

601
00:26:27,540 --> 00:26:28,380
What do you like?

602
00:26:28,380 --> 00:26:28,900
(Curious)

603
00:26:30,100 --> 00:26:31,900
I want to see new animals.

604
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:33,180
The wild ones.

605
00:26:34,020 --> 00:26:34,620
Wild ones like...

606
00:26:34,620 --> 00:26:36,580
giraffes, rhinos, and hippos.

607
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:39,580
And the dangerous ones too.

608
00:26:39,580 --> 00:26:41,340
Tigers, lions, all that.

609
00:26:41,820 --> 00:26:42,740
Anywhere else you want to go

610
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:43,340
besides the zoo?

611
00:26:43,860 --> 00:26:45,540
Have you been to Happy Valley?

612
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:46,900
Yeah, when I was little.

613
00:26:47,180 --> 00:26:48,540
You don't like it anymore,

614
00:26:48,540 --> 00:26:49,260
or what?

615
00:26:51,300 --> 00:26:52,300
I'm kind of scared.

616
00:26:53,300 --> 00:26:54,300
Of the scary rides?

617
00:26:56,900 --> 00:26:59,340
Like roller coasters?

618
00:26:59,940 --> 00:27:01,380
Would you ride one?

619
00:27:02,140 --> 00:27:03,020
I'm not scared.

620
00:27:03,220 --> 00:27:04,540
You're not? Wow.

621
00:27:05,260 --> 00:27:07,060
Maybe you were just too young then.

622
00:27:07,540 --> 00:27:08,700
Yeah, maybe.

623
00:27:08,700 --> 00:27:10,100
Maybe now that you're older,

624
00:27:10,100 --> 00:27:11,060
you're braver.

625
00:27:22,700 --> 00:27:24,620
(After Cui Kaiyi's exam)

626
00:27:26,180 --> 00:27:27,220
What's with the flowers?

627
00:27:27,220 --> 00:27:28,100
You did it.

628
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:30,940
They're so pretty.

629
00:27:32,340 --> 00:27:34,500
So many people inside
taking graduation photos.

630
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:35,500
Yeah, I saw.

631
00:27:35,500 --> 00:27:36,900
In their caps and gowns.

632
00:27:36,900 --> 00:27:37,620
Yeah.

633
00:27:38,180 --> 00:27:39,620
At your graduation,

634
00:27:39,620 --> 00:27:40,820
what color was the collar?

635
00:27:40,820 --> 00:27:41,860
Pink?

636
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:44,100
Ours had a floral pattern.

637
00:27:44,820 --> 00:27:45,700
A floral pattern?

638
00:27:45,980 --> 00:27:47,860
Yeah, new for our class.

639
00:27:47,860 --> 00:27:48,980
A new design?

640
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:50,940
What color was yours?

641
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:52,020
Dark blue.

642
00:27:52,020 --> 00:27:52,940
Dark blue?

643
00:27:53,700 --> 00:27:54,980
I want to see your graduation photos.

644
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:55,980
I bet you looked good.

645
00:27:55,980 --> 00:27:56,780
Okay.

646
00:27:57,140 --> 00:27:58,220
So, did you look good?

647
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:04,660
If you think so.

648
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:11,260
When do you get...

649
00:28:11,260 --> 00:28:11,980
My gown?

650
00:28:11,980 --> 00:28:12,860
Yeah, the gown.

651
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:14,740
Still waiting for it.

652
00:28:14,740 --> 00:28:15,820
Probably...

653
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:17,300
maybe...

654
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,500
another week or two.

655
00:28:21,150 --> 00:28:22,020
Do I get one too?

656
00:28:22,020 --> 00:28:23,060
You want one?

657
00:28:23,060 --> 00:28:24,340
Sure.

658
00:28:24,340 --> 00:28:25,460
Then wear one with me.

659
00:28:26,020 --> 00:28:28,860
But your pattern's hard to find.

660
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:31,180
Ours are solid colors.

661
00:28:31,180 --> 00:28:32,260
They're all white.

662
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:34,540
Then I'll match you.

663
00:28:34,540 --> 00:28:35,380
Okay.

664
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:35,940
That works.

665
00:28:43,300 --> 00:28:44,540
Do you argue much in relationships?

666
00:28:44,540 --> 00:28:45,260
(Asks)

667
00:28:45,260 --> 00:28:45,940
Argue?

668
00:28:49,260 --> 00:28:51,540
Anything you're really sensitive about?

669
00:28:51,540 --> 00:28:52,940
Sensitive about?

670
00:28:52,940 --> 00:28:55,060
Like something
you'd definitely fight over.

671
00:28:56,340 --> 00:28:57,620
(Looks)

672
00:28:57,980 --> 00:28:58,820
Definitely fight over...

673
00:28:58,820 --> 00:28:59,860
I get jealous pretty easily.

674
00:29:02,100 --> 00:29:03,220
Really? I wouldn't have guessed.

675
00:29:03,260 --> 00:29:05,060
(Laughs)

676
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:08,500
How jealous?

677
00:29:08,980 --> 00:29:11,140
Like I can't talk to anyone?

678
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:12,220
Not that bad.

679
00:29:12,860 --> 00:29:14,300
Funny, I remember you

680
00:29:14,300 --> 00:29:15,420
said on the patio

681
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,940
that you weren't the jealous type.

682
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:20,580
Was that you?

683
00:29:22,220 --> 00:29:23,060
Guess I remembered wrong.

684
00:29:26,780 --> 00:29:27,700
There are levels to it.

685
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:29,980
I'm not as jealous as I used to be.

686
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:31,260
As long as it's not intentional...

687
00:29:31,700 --> 00:29:33,220
You can usually tell.

688
00:29:34,540 --> 00:29:35,500
Anything else

689
00:29:36,420 --> 00:29:37,900
you think we'd fight about?

690
00:29:38,380 --> 00:29:40,660
Not really.

691
00:29:42,660 --> 00:29:45,140
I think the main thing is probably

692
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:46,500
(Time)
time.

693
00:29:46,860 --> 00:29:47,820
Time?

694
00:29:48,140 --> 00:29:49,980
School keeps me busy,

695
00:29:50,340 --> 00:29:52,220
so I may not

696
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:53,500
have much energy to give.

697
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:55,740
That causes fights.

698
00:29:55,740 --> 00:29:57,660
Yeah, when you're out of sync.

699
00:29:57,660 --> 00:29:58,540
I think so too.

700
00:29:58,540 --> 00:30:00,380
So how do you fix that?

701
00:30:00,940 --> 00:30:01,780
Stay busy.

702
00:30:02,020 --> 00:30:02,940
(Laughs)

703
00:30:02,940 --> 00:30:04,460
So, just keep yourself busy?

704
00:30:04,460 --> 00:30:05,540
Like, when you're busy,

705
00:30:05,540 --> 00:30:06,820
I'll do my own thing.

706
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:08,500
And when I'm busy, you do yours.

707
00:30:09,140 --> 00:30:10,540
You can't end the day

708
00:30:10,540 --> 00:30:12,900
with one person still wired

709
00:30:12,900 --> 00:30:14,500
and the other exhausted.

710
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:16,180
The worst part

711
00:30:16,180 --> 00:30:17,220
is when the energetic one

712
00:30:17,220 --> 00:30:17,900
doesn't get that...

713
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:19,340
Why the other one's exhausted.

714
00:30:19,940 --> 00:30:20,620
So yeah,

715
00:30:20,620 --> 00:30:22,660
have your own life too.

716
00:30:24,740 --> 00:30:26,100
Do you ever worry

717
00:30:26,740 --> 00:30:27,900
that if you don't see each other

718
00:30:28,580 --> 00:30:30,180
for too long,

719
00:30:30,180 --> 00:30:32,140
your feelings might fade?

720
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:33,380
(Asks)

721
00:30:35,020 --> 00:30:36,220
If we don't see each other,

722
00:30:36,220 --> 00:30:39,220
I think I'd miss you more.

723
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:40,140
Why?

724
00:30:41,140 --> 00:30:43,900
It just builds up.

725
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:46,820
You miss them more every day.

726
00:30:54,740 --> 00:30:55,340
I get that.

727
00:30:56,620 --> 00:30:58,700
If we were apart for a long time,

728
00:31:00,420 --> 00:31:01,340
would it fade?

729
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:02,540
I wouldn't let us

730
00:31:03,660 --> 00:31:04,540
stay apart that long.

731
00:31:04,540 --> 00:31:05,860
(We won't stay apart that long)

732
00:31:10,340 --> 00:31:12,620
Since you said

733
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:15,020
you get jealous,

734
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:16,980
what makes you

735
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:18,500
feel secure?

736
00:31:20,620 --> 00:31:21,860
I think

737
00:31:21,860 --> 00:31:24,020
these past few days with you

738
00:31:24,020 --> 00:31:26,460
have felt really secure.

739
00:31:29,180 --> 00:31:30,420
Then I'll keep that up.

740
00:31:30,420 --> 00:31:32,460
It's okay. Just...

741
00:31:32,460 --> 00:31:33,500
relax a little.

742
00:31:33,500 --> 00:31:35,340
I want you happy.

743
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:36,580
I already am.

744
00:31:36,580 --> 00:31:37,260
Yeah.

745
00:31:37,260 --> 00:31:38,300
If I can still be myself

746
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:40,900
and make you feel secure,
isn't that even better?

747
00:31:41,220 --> 00:31:41,900
Yeah.

748
00:31:53,700 --> 00:31:54,460
What're you making?

749
00:31:54,460 --> 00:31:56,420
Ginger-scallion crab.

750
00:31:56,860 --> 00:31:58,500
I can help clean them.

751
00:31:59,780 --> 00:32:00,740
Sure, why not?

752
00:32:01,780 --> 00:32:03,500
I'll chop some scallions.

753
00:32:03,900 --> 00:32:04,700
Sure.

754
00:32:13,140 --> 00:32:14,740
Just give it a quick rinse.

755
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:17,420
Chop these up?

756
00:32:17,820 --> 00:32:18,780
Yeah, chop them up.

757
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:20,300
Thanks.

758
00:32:20,300 --> 00:32:21,860
(Chops scallions)

759
00:32:27,060 --> 00:32:28,340
I'm heading upstairs.

760
00:32:28,340 --> 00:32:29,140
Go ahead.

761
00:32:31,820 --> 00:32:32,740
Is this enough?

762
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:34,220
That's enough.

763
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:34,700
Wow.

764
00:32:35,060 --> 00:32:36,040
(Impressed)
Perfect cuts.

765
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:37,700
Let me give it a quick rinse.

766
00:32:39,100 --> 00:32:40,500
I think...

767
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:42,780
maybe steam it first.

768
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:43,540
But they didn't...

769
00:32:43,540 --> 00:32:44,820
They said just pan-fry it.

770
00:32:45,580 --> 00:32:46,460
Ginger-scallion crab.

771
00:32:46,460 --> 00:32:48,420
Okay. I trust you.

772
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:48,900
(I'll trust you)

773
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:49,940
Trust me.

774
00:32:49,940 --> 00:32:51,020
I trust you.

775
00:32:53,060 --> 00:32:54,340
Early again?

776
00:32:54,700 --> 00:32:56,100
You're early too.

777
00:32:56,820 --> 00:32:57,300
It's just...

778
00:32:57,300 --> 00:32:58,380
I still feel late.

779
00:32:58,380 --> 00:32:59,540
I wanted food ready

780
00:32:59,540 --> 00:33:01,420
when everyone got here.

781
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:04,300
Hello.

782
00:33:04,820 --> 00:33:05,620
Hello.

783
00:33:05,940 --> 00:33:07,020
Grocery run?

784
00:33:07,020 --> 00:33:08,980
Yeah, a ton.

785
00:33:09,480 --> 00:33:10,000
Oh my God.

786
00:33:10,380 --> 00:33:11,980
We're making dumplings.

787
00:33:11,980 --> 00:33:12,580
What filling?

788
00:33:12,580 --> 00:33:13,820
Filling?

789
00:33:13,820 --> 00:33:14,780
Pork and celery.

790
00:33:19,060 --> 00:33:20,260
Hey, gorgeous.

791
00:33:20,260 --> 00:33:21,060
Hello.

792
00:33:21,060 --> 00:33:21,940
Have you eaten yet?

793
00:33:21,940 --> 00:33:22,820
Nope.

794
00:33:23,180 --> 00:33:24,340
You guys eat already?

795
00:33:25,100 --> 00:33:26,060
Nope, none of us.

796
00:33:26,060 --> 00:33:26,740
We just got back.

797
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:27,640
I knew it.

798
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:28,260
We haven't cooked yet.

799
00:33:28,260 --> 00:33:28,740
Not even started.

800
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:29,460
What are we making?

801
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:30,220
Dumplings.

802
00:33:30,220 --> 00:33:31,420
Dumplings today?

803
00:33:31,420 --> 00:33:32,300
From scratch.

804
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:33,340
It's New Year's again.

805
00:33:34,780 --> 00:33:35,660
Here we go.

806
00:33:35,660 --> 00:33:36,220
Okay.

807
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:40,500
Careful. Get the lid.

808
00:33:40,500 --> 00:33:40,940
We can just...

809
00:33:40,940 --> 00:33:41,820
Just pour it straight in.

810
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:43,820
(Helps)
Pour it in.

811
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:48,340
Perfect.

812
00:33:49,260 --> 00:33:50,060
Hello.

813
00:33:50,780 --> 00:33:51,140
Hello!

814
00:33:51,140 --> 00:33:51,620
Hello, guys.

815
00:33:51,620 --> 00:33:52,700
Hello.

816
00:33:53,060 --> 00:33:53,860
Hello.

817
00:33:54,140 --> 00:33:55,140
Hello.

818
00:33:55,140 --> 00:33:55,940
Have you eaten yet?

819
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:57,060
Have you eaten yet?

820
00:33:57,380 --> 00:33:59,060
No. Need any help?

821
00:33:59,060 --> 00:33:59,980
Help them with dumplings.

822
00:33:59,980 --> 00:34:01,020
I'm almost

823
00:34:01,020 --> 00:34:02,060
done here.

824
00:34:02,300 --> 00:34:03,340
Where can I help?

825
00:34:03,900 --> 00:34:04,940
Dumplings in a bit.

826
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:05,820
Okay.

827
00:34:06,220 --> 00:34:07,020
We're back.

828
00:34:07,220 --> 00:34:08,020
Hello.

829
00:34:08,500 --> 00:34:09,300
Hello.

830
00:34:10,580 --> 00:34:12,580
(Laughs)

831
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:13,540
Perfect timing.

832
00:34:13,540 --> 00:34:14,900
Five more minutes, and it's ready.

833
00:34:14,900 --> 00:34:15,580
Smell this.

834
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:16,860
I think it came out pretty well.

835
00:34:17,980 --> 00:34:18,820
My crab.

836
00:34:20,340 --> 00:34:21,300
Smells amazing!

837
00:34:21,740 --> 00:34:22,940
Your voice is cracking.

838
00:34:23,340 --> 00:34:24,900
It is not!

839
00:34:24,900 --> 00:34:25,820
It totally is.

840
00:34:25,820 --> 00:34:26,580
(Imitates)
Smells amazing.

841
00:34:27,220 --> 00:34:28,940
(Laughs)

842
00:34:30,940 --> 00:34:32,580
No gloves?

843
00:34:32,580 --> 00:34:34,260
No gloves.

844
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:35,540
I can't grip with gloves.

845
00:34:35,540 --> 00:34:37,380
They keep slipping.

846
00:34:39,820 --> 00:34:41,420
It smells kind of fishy.

847
00:34:41,420 --> 00:34:43,020
Yeah, super fishy.

848
00:34:45,980 --> 00:34:46,940
(Asks)
Not done yet?

849
00:34:46,940 --> 00:34:47,940
I think it needs...

850
00:34:48,340 --> 00:34:50,260
I need to turn up the heat
and let it cook down.

851
00:34:52,540 --> 00:34:53,580
Okay, I'll do that.

852
00:34:53,580 --> 00:34:55,460
Let the sauce thicken up.

853
00:35:00,860 --> 00:35:02,380
(Checks on her)

854
00:35:03,340 --> 00:35:05,180
Am I in the way?

855
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:06,180
Should I go?

856
00:35:06,180 --> 00:35:07,940
What? Sit down.

857
00:35:07,940 --> 00:35:09,460
Am I kind of third-wheeling here?

858
00:35:09,460 --> 00:35:10,308
No, you're fine.

859
00:35:10,308 --> 00:35:12,060
Just watch Cao Yiheng work his magic.

860
00:35:13,260 --> 00:35:15,700
Even his garlic looks good.

861
00:35:16,740 --> 00:35:18,180
Look how thin!

862
00:35:21,180 --> 00:35:22,500
Looks pretty good.

863
00:35:22,500 --> 00:35:23,380
Yeah, I think so.

864
00:35:23,820 --> 00:35:24,940
Not sure how it tastes, though.

865
00:35:28,260 --> 00:35:31,100
(Grabs chopsticks)

866
00:35:37,780 --> 00:35:38,660
Want to try it?

867
00:35:38,660 --> 00:35:39,740
Okay.

868
00:35:48,540 --> 00:35:49,340
Think it's done.

869
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:52,460
That's so good.

870
00:35:52,460 --> 00:35:53,740
This pan burned too.

871
00:35:53,740 --> 00:35:54,980
So that wasn't it.

872
00:35:54,980 --> 00:35:55,940
Dry-pot crab.

873
00:35:55,940 --> 00:35:56,680
We brought chopsticks,

874
00:35:56,680 --> 00:35:57,380
and he took away the plate.

875
00:35:57,380 --> 00:35:58,460
Look at this guy.

876
00:35:59,140 --> 00:36:00,820
He really "knows" what to do.

877
00:36:00,820 --> 00:36:01,580
Everyone, dig in.

878
00:36:01,580 --> 00:36:02,980
Eat here.

879
00:36:02,980 --> 00:36:04,140
Let's eat.

880
00:36:04,140 --> 00:36:05,260
Why did you

881
00:36:05,260 --> 00:36:06,100
move the plate?

882
00:36:06,100 --> 00:36:06,980
You two, sit.

883
